feat: CLAUDE_MEM_CLIENT_ONLY — use a worker another machine runs, never spawn/recycle/stop one

Marker: CLAUDE_MEM_CLIENT_ONLY

Several machines share one worker: the worker host runs it as usual, the others reach it through
`ssh -L 127.0.0.1:<port>:127.0.0.1:<port>` and set CLAUDE_MEM_CLIENT_ONLY=true. Upstream assumes
the worker on the port is its own, which splits the memory or drops data on a client:

- acquireSpawnLock() refuses: every launcher (hooks, start hook, MCP server, CLI restart) spawns only
  after winning it, so a client never starts a local worker with an empty DB on the tunnel's port.
  Callers then find no worker and report it unreachable (hook fail-loud counter, start-hook error).
- ensureWorkerRunning() does not recycle a worker on another plugin version (it would try to
  SIGKILL a process it does not own and drop the hook's data); the mismatch is only logged.
- httpShutdown() / shutdownWorkerAndWait() throw instead of stopping the shared worker.
- Any value but "true"/"false" is an error.
